# Scrollbars sit on the edge

Scrollbars must hug the scrollport’s inline-end (and block-end) border, like Cursor’s chat panel: thin overlay thumb, no gap between the track and the panel edge.

- The **scrollport** (`overflow: auto | overlay | scroll`) must not have padding on the side the scrollbar occupies. Prefer `padding-inline-end: 0` / `padding-right: 0`.
- Inset **content** instead: pad children, or shrink overlays (composer, values) with width/`padding` on the inner elements.
- Use the existing overlay treatment: `--lc-scrollbar-size` (4px), transparent track, `overflow-y: overlay` when available. Do not use `scrollbar-gutter: stable` (it reserves extra space and pulls the thumb inward).
- Parent chrome (header, composer) can stay inset; the scrolling layer still extends to the edge so the thumb can run the full height/width.

```css
/* ❌ BAD — padding on the scroller insets the thumb */
.scroll {
  overflow: auto;
  padding: 16px 12px;
}

/* ✅ GOOD — pad inner content; scroller is full-bleed */
.scroll {
  overflow: auto;
  padding: 16px 0;
}
.scroll > * {
  padding-inline-end: 12px;
}
```
